  "question": {
    "text": "The number of real solutions of the equation $x|x+5|+2|x+7|-2=0$ is_________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Case I : $x \\geq-5$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& x^2+5 x+2 x+12=0 \\\\\n& x^2+7 x+12=0 \\\\\n& x=-3,-4\n\\end{aligned}$\nCase II : $-7 < \\mathrm{x} < -5$\n$-x^2-5 x+2 x+14-2=0$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& -x^2-3 x+12=0 \\\\\n& x=\\frac{-3 \\pm \\sqrt{9+48}}{2} \\\\\n& =\\frac{-3 \\pm \\sqrt{57}}{2} \\\\\n& x=\\frac{-3-\\sqrt{57}}{2}, \\frac{-3+\\sqrt{57}}{2} \\text { (rejected) }\n\\end{aligned}$\nCase III : $\\mathrm{x} \\leq-7$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& -x^2-5 x-2 x-14-2=0 \\\\\n& x^2+7 x+16=0 \\\\\n& D=49-64 < 0\n\\end{aligned}$\nNo solutions\nNo. of solutions $=3$",
    "image": null
  },
